{"id":"p13-l09","minutes":35,"summary":"When the actuator saturates, the loop is effectively open, but a plain integrator keeps accumulating error and then has to unwind, which causes large overshoot and slow settling. You derive the two standard fixes, clamping (conditional integration) and back-calculation, implement both on the motor speed loop with a 12 volt limit, and test that each cuts the overshoot from a large step by more than a factor of five while leaving small, unsaturated steps untouched.","html":"<h2 id=\"windup\">Windup</h2>\n<p>A PI speed loop asked to jump from 0 to 200 rad/s starts with an error of 200 rad/s. With <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9694em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.12</span></span></span></span> it wants 24 V, but the driver can only give 12 V. While the voltage is pinned at the limit:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>the motor accelerates as fast as it can, regardless of the controller;</li>\n<li>the integrator keeps adding <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span></span></span></span> every step, storing a large voltage it can’t use.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>When the speed reaches its target the error turns negative, but the stored integral keeps the output saturated until the error has been negative long enough to unwind it. The result is a big overshoot, larger than the same loop shows without any limit.</p>\n<h2 id=\"clamping-conditional-integration\">Clamping (conditional integration)</h2>\n<p>Stop integrating while the output is saturated <strong>and</strong> the error would push it further into saturation:</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9202em;\"></span><span class=\"mord katex-accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9202em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span></span><span style=\"top:-3.2523em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.0278em;\"><span class=\"mord\">˙</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:3em;vertical-align:-1.25em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\"><span class=\"delimsizing size4\">{</span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"col-align-l\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.69em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.69em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.008em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.25em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.008em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.19em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:1em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-l\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.69em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.69em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.008em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">if </span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">u</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\"><span class=\"mrel\"><span class=\"mord katex-vbox\"><span class=\"katex-thinbox\"><span class=\"rlap\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-inner\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mrel\"></span></span></span><span class=\"katex-fix\"></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace nobreak\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\"> and </span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">sign</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">sign</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.25em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.008em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">otherwise</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.19em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>where <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span></span></span></span> is the controller’s unsaturated output and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">u</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">sat</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"back-calculation\">Back-calculation</h2>\n<p>Feed the saturation excess back into the integrator with time constant <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2806em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>:</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9202em;\"></span><span class=\"mord katex-accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9202em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span></span><span style=\"top:-3.2523em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.0278em;\"><span class=\"mord\">˙</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.1574em;vertical-align:-0.836em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.3214em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2806em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.836em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">u</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">v</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>While saturated, the integrator is pulled towards the value that would just reach the limit. A <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2806em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> a few times shorter than the integral time <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0361em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> works well. Back-calculation is smooth and easy to extend to rate limits; clamping is simplest to code.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"windup\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>A large speed step with the drive limited to 12 V, with no anti-windup, with clamping and with back-calculation. The plain integrator keeps charging while the voltage is pinned and then overshoots; both fixes stop it.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>The lab motor, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9694em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">p</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.12</span></span></span></span>, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">K</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2.5</span></span></span></span>, so <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">48</span></span></span></span> ms; limit 12 V; back-calculation with <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2806em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1389em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">t</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">20</span></span></span></span> ms.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>The steady voltage for 200 rad/s is <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">200/19.81</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">10.1</span></span></span></span> V, within the limit, so the target is reachable.</li>\n<li>Without a limit, this PI loop overshoots about 8 %.</li>\n<li>With the limit and no anti-windup the overshoot grows to about 18 %; with either fix it drops to about 1 %.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">antiwindup.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> numpy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">as</span> np\n\nR, L, k, J, b = <span class=\"hljs-number\">1.2</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.002</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.05</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2e-4</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2e-5</span>\nKp, Ki, Vmax, Tt = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.12</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2.5</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">12.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.02</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">run</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">mode, w_ref=<span class=\"hljs-number\">200.0</span>, T=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1.5</span>, dt=<span class=\"hljs-number\">5e-5</span>, limit=<span class=\"hljs-literal\">True</span></span>):\n    i = w = I = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>; ws = []\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> _ <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>(T / dt)):\n        e = w_ref - w\n        v = Kp * e + I                                     <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># unsaturated controller output</span>\n        u = np.clip(v, -Vmax, Vmax) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> limit <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span> v\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> mode == <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;none&quot;</span>:\n            I += Ki * e * dt\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">elif</span> mode == <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;clamp&quot;</span>:\n            <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">not</span> (u != v <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> np.sign(e) == np.sign(v)):\n                I += Ki * e * dt\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">elif</span> mode == <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;back&quot;</span>:\n            I += (Ki * e + (u - v) / Tt) * dt\n        f = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">lambda</span> s: np.array([(u - R * s[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>] - k * s[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>]) / L, (k * s[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>] - b * s[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>]) / J])\n        s = np.array([i, w])\n        k1 = f(s); k2 = f(s + dt / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * k1); k3 = f(s + dt / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * k2); k4 = f(s + dt * k3)\n        i, w = s + dt / <span class=\"hljs-number\">6</span> * (k1 + <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * k2 + <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * k3 + k4); ws.append(w)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> np.array(ws)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">overshoot</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">w, ref</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>, (w.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() - ref) / ref)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">settle</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">w, ref, dt=<span class=\"hljs-number\">5e-5</span>, band=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.02</span></span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> (np.where(np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(w - ref) &gt; band * ref)[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>][-<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>] + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) * dt\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_windup_and_fixes</span>():\n    lin = overshoot(run(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;none&quot;</span>, limit=<span class=\"hljs-literal\">False</span>), <span class=\"hljs-number\">200</span>)\n    res = {m: run(m) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> m <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> (<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;none&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;clamp&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;back&quot;</span>)}\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;no limit: overshoot <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{lin:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>%}</span>&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> m, w <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> res.items():\n        <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;12 V limit, <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{m:5s}</span>: overshoot <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{overshoot(w, <span class=\"hljs-number\">200</span>):<span class=\"hljs-number\">5.1</span>%}</span>, settles in <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{settle(w, <span class=\"hljs-number\">200</span>) * <span class=\"hljs-number\">1000</span>:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.0</span>f}</span> ms&quot;</span>)\n    os_none = overshoot(res[<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;none&quot;</span>], <span class=\"hljs-number\">200</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> os_none &gt; lin                                   <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># windup is worse than no limit at all</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> m <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> (<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;clamp&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;back&quot;</span>):\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> overshoot(res[m], <span class=\"hljs-number\">200</span>) &lt; os_none / <span class=\"hljs-number\">5</span>\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> settle(res[m], <span class=\"hljs-number\">200</span>) &lt; settle(res[<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;none&quot;</span>], <span class=\"hljs-number\">200</span>)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_small_steps_untouched</span>():\n    ws = [run(m, w_ref=<span class=\"hljs-number\">40.0</span>, T=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.6</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> m <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> (<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;none&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;clamp&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;back&quot;</span>)]\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>(np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">40.0</span> * <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.12</span>)) &lt; Vmax                <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># never saturates: Kp*e starts at 4.8 V</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> np.allclose(ws[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>], ws[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>]) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> np.allclose(ws[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>], ws[<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>])\n\ntest_windup_and_fixes()\ntest_small_steps_untouched()\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;PASS&quot;</span>)</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why does clamping check the sign of the error, instead of freezing the integrator whenever the output is saturated?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>If the output is saturated high but the error has turned negative, integrating helps: it brings the output back out of saturation sooner. Freezing it there would leave the stored integral stuck at its saturated value and delay recovery.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>A controller runs on a microcontroller whose PWM duty saturates at 95 %, but the anti-windup uses a 100 % limit. What happens?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>Between 95 % and 100 % the anti-windup thinks it’s unsaturated and keeps integrating while the real actuator is pinned, so windup returns in that band. The anti-windup must use the true actuator limit, ideally the value actually applied.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p13-l09\"></div>\n","toc":[{"id":"windup","title":"Windup"},{"id":"clamping-conditional-integration","title":"Clamping (conditional integration)"},{"id":"back-calculation","title":"Back-calculation"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p13-l09-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Voltage in V the PI asks for at the first instant of a 200 rad/s step with K_p = 0.12?</p>\n","explain":"<p>K_p e, before any integral.</p>\n","answer":24,"tol":0.001,"unit":"V"},{"id":"p13-l09-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Integral time T_i in ms for K_p = 0.12 and K_i = 2.5?</p>\n","explain":"<p>K_p/K_i.</p>\n","answer":48,"tol":0.001,"unit":"ms"},{"id":"p13-l09-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Steady voltage in V needed for 200 rad/s with a DC gain of 19.81 (rad/s)/V?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Within the 12 V limit.</p>\n","answer":10.1,"tol":0.003,"unit":"V"},{"id":"p13-l09-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Largest step in rad/s that doesn’t saturate a 12 V drive at the first instant with K_p = 0.12?</p>\n","explain":"<p>K_p e ≤ V_max.</p>\n","answer":100,"tol":0.001,"unit":"rad/s"},{"id":"p13-l09-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>Back-calculation drives the integrator using…</p>\n","explain":"<p>(u − v)/T_t.</p>\n","options":["the difference between the saturated and unsaturated output","the derivative of the error","the motor current","a separate model"],"answer":0},{"id":"p13-l09-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>Without anti-windup, saturation typically causes…</p>\n","explain":"<p>The stored integral has to unwind.</p>\n","options":["larger overshoot and slower settling","zero overshoot","faster settling","a steady error"],"answer":0}],"code":[{"file":"antiwindup.py","lang":"python","src":"import numpy as np\n\nR, L, k, J, b = 1.2, 0.002, 0.05, 2e-4, 2e-5\nKp, Ki, Vmax, Tt = 0.12, 2.5, 12.0, 0.02\n\ndef run(mode, w_ref=200.0, T=1.5, dt=5e-5, limit=True):\n    i = w = I = 0.0; ws = []\n    for _ in range(int(T / dt)):\n        e = w_ref - w\n        v = Kp * e + I                                     # unsaturated controller output\n        u = np.clip(v, -Vmax, Vmax) if limit else v\n        if mode == \"none\":\n            I += Ki * e * dt\n        elif mode == \"clamp\":\n            if not (u != v and np.sign(e) == np.sign(v)):\n                I += Ki * e * dt\n        elif mode == \"back\":\n            I += (Ki * e + (u - v) / Tt) * dt\n        f = lambda s: np.array([(u - R * s[0] - k * s[1]) / L, (k * s[0] - b * s[1]) / J])\n        s = np.array([i, w])\n        k1 = f(s); k2 = f(s + dt / 2 * k1); k3 = f(s + dt / 2 * k2); k4 = f(s + dt * k3)\n        i, w = s + dt / 6 * (k1 + 2 * k2 + 2 * k3 + k4); ws.append(w)\n    return np.array(ws)\n\ndef overshoot(w, ref):\n    return max(0.0, (w.max() - ref) / ref)\n\ndef settle(w, ref, dt=5e-5, band=0.02):\n    return (np.where(np.abs(w - ref) > band * ref)[0][-1] + 1) * dt\n\ndef test_windup_and_fixes():\n    lin = overshoot(run(\"none\", limit=False), 200)\n    res = {m: run(m) for m in (\"none\", \"clamp\", \"back\")}\n    print(f\"no limit: overshoot {lin:.1%}\")\n    for m, w in res.items():\n        print(f\"12 V limit, {m:5s}: overshoot {overshoot(w, 200):5.1%}, settles in {settle(w, 200) * 1000:.0f} ms\")\n    os_none = overshoot(res[\"none\"], 200)\n    assert os_none > lin                                   # windup is worse than no limit at all\n    for m in (\"clamp\", \"back\"):\n        assert overshoot(res[m], 200) < os_none / 5\n        assert settle(res[m], 200) < settle(res[\"none\"], 200)\n\ndef test_small_steps_untouched():\n    ws = [run(m, w_ref=40.0, T=0.6) for m in (\"none\", \"clamp\", \"back\")]\n    assert np.max(np.abs(40.0 * 0.12)) < Vmax                # never saturates: Kp*e starts at 4.8 V\n    assert np.allclose(ws[0], ws[1]) and np.allclose(ws[0], ws[2])\n\ntest_windup_and_fixes()\ntest_small_steps_untouched()\nprint(\"PASS\")"}]}